   "Drafts were reviewed against repository source before use; the review found and fixed four defects in the instrument, not in Cartograph.",
   "GAP-1 (an unrecognised decorator receiver) was being applied to Django path() entries, which have no receiver. It now applies only to decorator forms.",
   "Handlers for Django URL-conf entries were being read as 'the next def in the file', which attributed an unrelated admin helper to a route. The view is now read from the entry's second argument.",
   "Records whose path could not be recovered are marked INSTRUMENT_NO_PATH and excluded from every denominator, rather than being counted as routes or silently dropped.",
   "path(..., include(...)) is a mount point, not a route (OUT-10); a view named through csrf_exempt/admin_view/as_view is marked handler_resolvable=false, so the route counts but the chain cannot.",
   "ORM flavour is decided by what a class declares (__tablename__ vs Meta.db_table), not by its base name: `Model` alone is used by both Django and Flask-AppBuilder, and attributing it by name mislabelled all 32 Superset models and all 61 Airflow models as Django."
